From: Djair Guilherme <djair.jr@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: cv1800: gadget buffer DMA, no descriptor DMA

dwc2_set_cv1800_params() turns gadget DMA off (g_dma = false) but leaves
the default g_dma_desc, which requires g_dma, so dwc2_check_params()
warns "Invalid parameter g_dma_desc=1" at every probe.

Use buffer DMA and keep descriptor DMA off. Measured on the reCamera
(SG2002, NCM gadget, iperf3 against a Linux host):
  slave mode (no DMA):          host->dev 122 Mbit/s, dev->host  94 Mbit/s
  buffer DMA:                   host->dev 157 Mbit/s, dev->host 146 Mbit/s
  buffer + descriptor DMA:      dev->host TCP stalls (ICMP still passes)
Buffer DMA also moved 200 MB each way over ssh with matching md5 and no
dwc2 errors.

diff --color -ruN a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c	2026-10-18 16:35:53.180475731 -0300
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c	2026-10-18 16:35:53.196851915 -0300
@@ -225,7 +225,8 @@
 	p->otg_caps.hnp_support = false;
 	p->otg_caps.srp_support = false;
 	p->host_dma = false;
-	p->g_dma = false;
+	p->g_dma = true;
+	p->g_dma_desc = false;	/* descriptor DMA stalls dev->host NCM TCP */
 	p->speed = DWC2_SPEED_PARAM_HIGH;
 	p->phy_type = DWC2_PHY_TYPE_PARAM_UTMI;
 	p->phy_utmi_width = 16;
